Just wanted to say that after dozens of dead monks, several who died
by the hand of Kaen, I've managed to kill the guy! (slightly spoily
stuff below, but I think anyone could figure out this plan).

I'd almost consider this a gaming feat higher than my first ascension.
My plan was to go in with some blessed scrolls of earth to protect me
and a ring of conflict and have the Xorns/Earth Elementals work for
me. It didn't quite work out that way. For whatever reason, they
wouldn't attack the meditating Kaen. So... after beating up all the
Xorns/Earth Elementals from within my ad hoc fort, I carefully pushed
a boulder out so I had a line of sight to zap Kaen with a sleep spell.
The first time I missed. The second time I hit. I cautiously
approached, and then bludgeoned him with Mjollnir about 5 times before
he woke up and teleported to the up stairs.

I stepped into his line of sight again (going for sleep ray #2), and
he ran up the stairs. I followed, zapped him with the sleep ray, two
more hits with the hammer and he was down. He didn't have time to hit
me once, with spell or fist.

Someday I'll try this hand-to-hand, no cheating with sleep rays or
boulders, but in the meanwhile, wow, that felt good.

